  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Optum Public Sector Solutions obligated $19.9B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The vendor won 30 awards so far, with an average award size of $664M. Obligations fell 11.5% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $8.9B in FY21 to $22.5B in FY25, then moved to $19.9B in FY26. The FY21 through FY26 series shows a multiyear growth phase followed by a partial-year pullback in the current fiscal year. Current-year totals are partial, and the published note clarifies that contract obligations are the measure used except where award-value figures are explicitly called out as total contract values. Readers should treat the FY2026 figure as fiscal year to date rather than a full-year total. The dataset reports counts and averages alongside the dollar totals, making award-level scale visible through the $664M average award size and the 30-award tally for the current year.",
